PARSE.INSTRUCTIONS - handoff for a new Claude session (paste this file as
the first message, attach the current source files)
===========================================================================

WHO / WHAT
  Jonas's IVM: a bytecode VM + a 6502 JIT + a grammar-driven C compiler.
  Targets: sim65 (sim6502) and Oric Atmos; cc65 device builds (ivm-jit.sim,
  parse.sim). Goals: SMALL code (cc65 binary size), then speed. Prefer
  rules / templates / grammar (data) over C code: remove C where possible.

MY RULES (always)
  - Deliver FULL files (Claude edits with small replacements, sending a
    full file costs nothing extra). Keep my formatting; don't touch
    unrelated lines.
  - Every code "paragraph" gets a 1-2 word comment (like naming a
    subroutine), blank lines between groups. Keep spacious comments.
  - Comments: terse but spacious, to the point. Plain sentences and
    short "- " lists, a blank line between thoughts; say where it
    applies ("on for ./pc (host), off in ./parse"). NOT dense
    colon-chained brain dumps ("X: y (z: w), else ..."). E.g.:
      // IVM_OPT: -O  = include optimizer that does various things:
      // - layout (frame packing)
      // - gen_pack
      // - gen_optimize
      //
      // It's default and included on HOST builds using ./pc
      // Using ./parse it's off
  - Includes: #include "file.c", no .h files (unless for "users").
    A file's own main() goes under #ifndef MAIN.
  - cc65 compiles all code it sees, used or not: anything not needed
    on the 6502 goes under an #ifdef (measure: cc65 -S + ca65 -l).
  - Lists and anything with structure: one item per line, never a
    dense run of text (a | b | c ..., "x: y, z: w ..."). Sections like
    lib tiers: the -- cut N -- lines and each routine on its own line.
    The same in comments, docs, MEMMAP output and replies.
  - Tables in .md files: aligned in the source too (columns padded,
    numbers right aligned, | under |): readable in a terminal. A short
    name first (the test), the numbers, the long text (the code) last.
    ./mdtoc FILE.md aligns them (and the linked index of the headings).
  - No magic numbers: named constants.
  - Asm comments: whole line ;;;  inline ;;
  - cc65 C89: declarations before statements; no ?: in case labels
    (cc65: "constant integer expression expected"). Check with gcc:
      gcc -fsyntax-only -Wall -Wno-unused -Wdeclaration-after-statement \
        -Ix2/stub -DJIT -DNOHOSTSIM -DMEMMAP [-D__SIM6502__|-D__ATMOS__] \
        -D_heapmaxavail\(\)=1000 -D'__asm__(...)=' ivm.c
      (x2/stub/disasm.c is an empty file; plain -DJIT on gcc = HOSTSIM)
  - Save code BYTES: no clever packing / conversion macros (an index is
    letter - 'A', a name is 'A' + r); prefer isalpha() etc. over chains
    of compares. Measure cc65 sizes (I do, on Termux).
  - Be concise. Tests in the descriptive format (see TESTS).
  - zj naming in ivm-print.c stays. The grammar file is c.bnf (C), p.bnf
    (Pascal).
  - Work only in Claude's own workspace (fresh mktemp dirs), never on my
    device; no destructive commands.

FILES
  ivm.c         VM + JIT driver (layout, -o image writer, in-place loader,
                MEMMAP). JIT_6502 build drops the VM (NOIVM-like block).
  ivm-jit.c     6502 JIT: rule tables (op, guard, post state, template),
                emit_tpl, init folding, host simulator path (HOSTSIM).
  ivm-lib.asm   runtime lib (ca65), tiers + cuts, startup parts.
  ivm-vm.asm    6502 VM (asm).
  cpu6502.c drv.c  host 6502 sim + JIT test driver (gcc -O2 -DHOSTSIM).
  parse.c       grammar engine + C/Pascal front end (gcc -O2 -o parse;
                -DSYMS writes NAME.sym).
  bnf2bin.c     the grammar: format, rule[], loads c.bnf.bin (all
                targets). BNF_TEXT (host only): reads c.bnf, writes
                the .bin (./parse.x -B c.bnf, or ./bnf2bin.x c.bnf).
                The 6502 parse.sim only loads c.bnf.bin; on 6502 the
                alt tables are relocated in place (no malloc).
  c.bnf p.bnf   grammars.  ivm-gen.c  emitter / consts / symbols / blob.
  ivm-walk.c    opcode table.  ivm-print.c  .ivm listing.  parse-syms.c
  bnfconv.py    one-off: old grammars (A..Z rule calls) -> $X syntax.

GRAMMAR ENCODING (parse.c, current)
  Rule calls are $A..$Z, $a..$z (minor helpers, same letter as the rule
  they help); defined as X= / x= at a line start. Plain letters in a
  pattern are literals (literals match case-insensitively: ignore_case 1).
  Rule index = letter - 'A' (NRULES 'z'-'A'+1, a few unused slots).
  Bytes: plain ASCII literal; $81-$9A letter directives \a..\z (HIDIR);
  $A0-$C0 ws gap + punct/digit directives (HIBIT); $C1-$DA / $E1-$FA rule
  calls (HIBIT(letter), IS_RULE); $DB $DD production [ ]; $FB $FD \{ \}.
  \< = 2 bytes: HIBIT('<'), $20 + alt (1..31; $20 = whole rule again).
  \> marks the jump target alt. \! statement error recovery. \% skip a
  false #if branch. \j no temp after a plain load. \xHH exact byte.
  \@ \$ \: \, \. arrays (make, sizeof, init). \c const, \g init.
  \"text" prints text on its own line, once per source place (rule L:
  the &x warning). Free directive chars: ` only.

OPTIMIZATIONS (ivm-gen.c; impact: MeteoriC-man.md "Optimizations", test-opts.c)
  - IVM_OPT (-O: layout, gen_pack, gen_optimize = peephole + squeeze):
    on for host (./pc), off in cc65 parse.sim (-DIVM_OPT: 3.6 KB).
  - IVM_CSE (gen_deadload, gen_swap): host only (-DIVM_CSE: 3.5 KB).
  - Value numbering (vn_temp, while emitting): always (-DIVM_NO_VN).
    &x in the code + a slot kept over a pointer store (vn_risk): main
    compiles again with vn_alias (init() resets all compile state).
  - Idea: move -O to a separate ./ivm-opt (.ivm in, .ivm out).

C FRONT END STATE (c.bnf)
  - Precedence: left to right, an operator may only be followed by the
    same or a looser level (\> \<): * / %, + -, << >>, < <= > >=, == !=,
    &, ^, |. a + b * c is an ERROR (needs parens). ! binds tight.
  - Error recovery: a statement / declaration / function that fails is
    reported (file:line, caret, undefined name), skipped (to ; or over a
    {} block, with else), parsing goes on; at the end "--- N errors ---",
    no .ivm, exit 1.
  - Preprocessor (rule Q, top level and blocks): #define N number|"str",
    #ifdef/#ifndef NAME, #if 0 / #if N, #else, #endif; other # lines
    skipped. Predefined (made when first used): __MC65__ = .ivm version
    (mark bytes 2,3: 'M',0 = 19712), __TARGET_6502__ = 1. _ starts names.
  - static/extern prefixes, fflush(stdout), getchar() (op K; JIT rule
    calls lib getchar, last lib tier).
  - Static arrays (bss, zeroed at startup / by sim65), initialized arrays
    (data). Unused plain consts are dropped from the .ivm.

JIT / IMAGE STATE
  - Lib tiers (ivm-lib.asm). An image ends at the cut after the highest
    routine its code calls (lc_libtop; re-layout if it needs more):

      startup parts (see below)
      -- cut 0 --
      memset          (the startup's bss zeroing calls it)
      -- cut 1 --
      putchar
      printstr        (")
      puts            (P)
      -- cut 2 --
      putnum          (.)
      -- cut 3 --
      mul
      mod
      div
      -- cut 4 --
      malloc
      free
      -- cut 5 --
      getchar
      -- cut 6 --
      args           (x / y's arguments)
      move
      strlen
      strcmp
      strncmp
      memcmp
      strchr
      memchr
      strcpy
      strncpy
      -- cut 7 --
      putf ...        (513 B, below)
      -- end --

  - putf, printf's parts (cut 7). The arguments:
      AX   the value (u d x X), the string's address (s)
      Y    the width, signed: 4 is %4, -4 is %-4 (left aligned)
    The control block, 0 = default, every putf sets it back to 0:
      _ivmlib_pfpad     the pad char (0: space)
      _ivmlib_pfprec    .N (0: none)
    Kept between calls:
      _ivmlib_pfcount   chars printed (putfn: AX = it, putfn0: 0)
      _ivmlib_pfout     the output routine (putfout; 0: putchar)
    The routines:
      putfu putfd putfx putfX putfs     the value
      putfuz ... putfsz                 the value, then the string after
                                        the JSR
      putfz                             only the string after the JSR
    ACC is not kept.
    Next: lib ids for x / y from 32, the compiler splitting printf.

  - Startup parts. An image starts at the first one it needs:
      _ivmlib_init      bss zeroed (memset)
      _ivmlib_zpclr     -z: zero the live mem[] the image doesn't carry
      _ivmlib_zpinit    -z: copy the mem[] image to zp
      _ivmlib_start     $00-$01 = 00 00 (NULL reads 0); sim65: ldx #$FF
                        txs; then jsr the code
      _ivmlib_exit      sim65: jmp exit, Atmos: rts (to BASIC)
    Their operands are patched by ivm.c / ivm-image.c.

  - Image: consts not in mem[] (immediates; lc_kread re-layout if read).
    -z: mem[] image after the code, only up to its last non-0 byte on a
    sim65 file (memory starts zeroed; also no bss zeroing then).
  - Zero page:
      sim65:
        $00-$01   NULL: 00 00 (_ivmlib_start; also ivm.c's main)
        $02-$03   CSP: cc65's sp, sim65's arg pointer (header byte 7);
                  zp from $02 in mklib and sim6502.cfg
        $04-$09   ivm-lib: ptr1 ptr2 tmp3 tmp4 (tmp1/2 sreg: aliases)
        $0A-$F9   -z mem[] (from _ivmlib_zplo, below zptop $FA)
        $FC-$FF   JIT: array element pointer, scratch (tmp1 tmp2)
      Atmos:
        $00-$01   NULL: 00 00 (the ROM / BASIC don't use $00-$0B)
        $E2-$FB   ivm-lib: cc65's zero page (zeropage.inc)
        $FC-$FF   JIT, as sim65
    pvio: a static arg frame, no C stack.
  - Results: test-empty.ivm.sim 33 B (cl65 191, Oscar 137), test-const
    63 B, byte-sieve-array 437 B.

TESTS
  ./run.sh OUT   : every t/*.c, plain and -O, VM (ivmh) vs JIT (drv) and
                   drv -z; "fails: 0" expected; compare .ivm bytes and
                   jit B / cycles against the previous run (no regressions).
  ./te/run-err.sh: te/*.c must NOT compile; lines marked "// ERR" must be
                   exactly the reported error lines; no .ivm.
  Test file format (like t/test-incdec.c): a header explaining what is
  tested, why, the expected results; each case
     printf("name:\texpected\n\t\t");  then the actual values, printf("\n")
  gcc on the same file is the reference where possible.

OPEN / NEXT: JIT loops (test-loop-*.c, ./ptest 'loop-*')
  - The family: one loop form each, same work (10000 rounds). Cycles
    per round = (cycles - test-empty's) / 10000. Table and findings:
    MeteoriC-man.md "Loop forms, measured".
  - Done (2026-11): the JIT's loop test always leaves the loop var in
    AX (ivm-jit.c 't' 'u': ax = 1); x = x + y, x = y + x (int) are
    U x y in c.bnf (-133 bytes on all the tests, asm loops -24%).
  - JIT: U a b with ACC = mem[b] known (the loop var) could be
    clc / adc a / sta a / txa / adc a+1 / sta a+1: 2 cycles.
  - JIT: <= (t) costs the same as < (u). A limit in a slot costs 4
    (a variable), 6 (N - 1: computed at run time; fold it?).
  - ACC contract: t u n as SLOT (ACC = the loop var at the body), not
    UNDEF. The VM does it already, the JIT now too. Then the
    interpreters can drop a body's first <i> (test-loop-for-acc).
  - Interpreters: for is the fastest form; down / postdec / while-expr
    have no loop op (a down-counting op? ask first: op letters).

OPEN / NEXT: JIT, keep values in ACC (easiest first)
  ACC is the value, its place A/X or A/Y (Y lo, A hi). The JIT has
  A/X (acc_at, acc_s) and A/Y only in stride loops (lc_yas).

  1. U a b with ACC = mem[b] known (the loop var): use it, no load.
  2. Compares that jump (u t as if, < = > before G / zjp) and whose 0/1
     result nobody reads: branch on the flags (high byte first) and
     keep ACC = the first value. if (a < 32) ... a: no reload on either
     path (f(int a) today: sta, lda cmp lda sbc, then lda ldx again on
     both paths). Pays most in small recursive functions.
  3. Rotate zj ... J B loops (down counting): the test at the bottom,
     J's dec flags as the test. test-loop-down 45 -> about 30 (oscar).
  4. Delayed write (a "dirty" ACC, as in my lisp compiler): S s doesn't
     store, ACC = mem[s] (in A/X or A/Y) marked dirty. The JIT has the delayed LOAD
     already (ACC_PEND); this is the other half. Write it out before:
     A/X gets a new value; anything reads mem[s] not via ACC; a call;
     a pointer read/store (with lc_alias); labels and jumps (all paths
     must agree). Wins: S s ... S s (first store gone), a value used
     right after its store, and loops: carried over the back jump, a
     loop's accumulator in a register till the exit (oscar's win: s in
     Y/X, i in zp, 30 cycles a round against our 39).
  5. ACC at joins (my lisp compiler): at a label, if every path into it
     ends with the same ACC (the same var, the same place, dirty or
     not), keep knowing it, else "don't know". Today acc_label() always
     forgets (only a while head, lc_ksa, makes its back jump agree).
     Forward jumps: their state is known when emitted. A loop head:
     assume the entry's, make the back jump agree (a load / move before
     it), as lc_ksa does.

OPEN / NEXT: run constant code at compile time (host, ivm-opt)
  - Track known slot values while generating (the peephole's kc / kv
    for ACC, extended to slots): known after a constant store,
    unknown after anything else.
  - A loop with only known inputs that writes only slots (no calls,
    I/O, pointer stores): run it in the compiler (parse.x has the VM,
    -DRUN), a step limit. Replace it by constant stores of each slot
    it wrote (the loop var too) and the last ACC.
  - That's oscar's 0.5 cycles a round on test-loop-count.

OPEN / NEXT: slot promotion (some day, an -O saving)
  - Give the 32 one byte load slots (0..31) to the vars that use L xx
    the most. Score per var: its L xx count (= bytes saved), +30 for
    each L xx inside a loop (a backward B / n jump's range).
  - Measured (2026-11): xx instead of L xx saves 1 byte, and per load
    run: ivm-asm / ivm-fix 8 cycles, the C ivm 83.
  - Layout stays: [promoted globals][other globals][frames, contiguous]
    [globals after][consts]. Locals are not promoted (for now).
  - gen_pack already lays globals out from 0 (frames right after): in
    small programs everything is < 32. It only matters past 32 slots.
  - The counting: ivm-count has it; gen_pack would order by the score.

OPEN / NEXT (imacs.c port; easiest first)
  - Grammar-only: do K while (E); *(E) *--p *p--; unary minus; ?:;
    && || (short circuit); assignment in expressions (c = getch());
    T name[] params; puts(E); #define NAME (expr).
  - Small C: break/continue (patch stack per loop); printf format split at
    compile time (%d %u %s %c, widths ignored); real static locals.
  - Bigger: signed compares (x < 0 hi bit; int vs unsigned type), structs
    (fields as consts in their own namespace, p->f = word index;
    constructor = call-like store of args, last in ACC), #include, a small
    libc in our C (strlen memmove memcpy strncpy isalnum isspace atoi).
  - Offered earlier: X-macro rule table (~220 B), rule hit counter, loop
    alignment (qsort), char loop vars as byte index, int array types,
    skip frame header cells (slot map), FR_ACC store only with params,
    entry straight to main (skip JMP _start trampoline), drop ldx/txs if
    sim65 starts SP=$FF, error messages naming "if" as undefined.
